.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-admin-operators-revoke - Remove an account's operator role (write mode, audited)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 admin operators revoke  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove the operator role from an account: from its next request it is a merchant
account like any other, and a write-mode token it holds stops working with it. The
argument is the ACCOUNT's id, as 'rail0 admin operators' lists it. The grant is deleted;
the audit log keeps who granted it and who revoked it.

.PP
The gateway refuses two cases. Your own grant: stepping down is another operator's act,
so the role cannot be dropped by a slip, nor by a stolen session covering its tracks. And
the last active operator: someone must be able to grant the role again.

.PP
The command reads the account and asks, naming it.

.PP
A write: it needs write mode ('rail0 admin write-mode on').


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for revoke

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip the confirmation prompt (required to run non-interactively)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 admin operators revoke 019e748b-…
  rail0 admin operators revoke 019e748b-… --yes
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-admin-operators(1)\fP
